      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "नीरागेषु—S'iva, though the greatest of lovers, is also greater than",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the greatest of those who have renounced the world; for he only",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "could do the two opposite things, viz. to yield to the in-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "fluence of love so far as to allow his wife to share half of his",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "body and also to resist successfully the action of the shafts",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "of Káma which are irresitsible दुर्वार to others Cf. न रागि चेतः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "परमा विलासिता वधूः शरीरेऽस्ति न चास्ति मन्मथः । Kir. XVIII. 31.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "विभूषणोद्भासि पिनद्धभोगि वा गजाजिनालम्बि दुकूलधारि वा । कपालि वा स्या-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "दथवेन्दुशेखरं न विश्वमूर्तेरवधार्यते वपुः ॥ Kum V. 73. ॰व्याविद्धमुग्ध—lying",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "in a stupor, the poison having pervaded the body शेषः—other",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "than S'iva. Ordinary people never enjoy pleasures ( as they",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "would do, for they are only कामविडम्बित ) and also are not able",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "to renounce them.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 19. For माहात्म्यम् some read दाहात्म्यम् which is equivalent",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "to दाहात्मकताम्—power to burn. माहात्म्यम् can also be easily",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "understood from the context to mean the same thing. बडिशयुतम्",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "—to which a fish-hook is attached. बडिशं मत्स्यवेधनम् । Amara.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "The moth and the fish are not gifted with the faculty of discern-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "ment and they cannot perceive danger, but men, reasoning",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "beings that they are, are ruined by their desires. जटिल–inter-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "twined, complicated. गहनः– inscrutable, mysterious.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 20. वलित—mixed with. प्रतीकारो व्याधे. सुखम्—The remo-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "val of pain is happiness. Really, there is no such thing as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "happiness says the poet. What is felt to be as such is merely",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "on account of the pain being removed. विपर्यस्यति wrongly",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "thinks; see com.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 21. तुङ्गं &c.–These, singly or together. कल्याणी-कल्यं नीरु-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "जत्वमाणयतीति; fortunate: cf. त्वमेव कल्याणि तयोस्तृतीया । Rag. VI. 29.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "निविशते–sticks fondly or closely to: विश् with नि is Atm. ‘नेर्विशः’",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "Pân. I. 3. 17. संसारकारागृह – कारागृह of course to a philosopher.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "धन्यः &c —यः संन्यस्यति स धन्यः । संन्यास means abandoning all",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "desire; Cf. काम्यानां कर्मणां न्यासं संन्यासं कवयो विदुः । Bg. XVIII. 2.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 22. The adjectives in the first two lines require to be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "distributed between शिशुकैः and गेहिनी according as they are in",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
